  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Unpolarised light is incident on the boundary between two dielectric media, whose dielectric constants are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math> (medium &ndash;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>) and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math> (medium &ndash; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>), respectively. To satisfy the condition, so that the reflected and refracted rays are perpendicular to each other, the angle of incidence should be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>,&nbsp;the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;is ______.</p><p>(Given for dielectric media, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As given in the question, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;and</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Now applying Snell&#39;s law and considering&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>i</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}